    "A <link rel=\"me\"> in the page's <head> does the same, and rel=\"me noopener\" counts as well: the server looks for \"me\" among the rel words of any anchor or link on the page. The address has to be your own profile address, the one in the line above; a trailing slash or a #fragment makes no difference." : "Nì <link rel=\"me\"> ann an <head> na duilleige an aon rud, agus cunntaidh rel=\"me noopener\" cuideachd: lorgaidh am frithealaiche \"me\" am measg faclan rel ceangail no acair sam bith air an duilleag. Feumaidh an seòladh a bhith ’na sheòladh na pròifil agad fhèin, am fear air an loidhne gu h-àrd; chan eil diofar ma tha slais no #bloigh air an deireadh.",
    "This server fetches the page itself, in the background, at most once a day per account, over http or https only, and reads the first part of it. A page it cannot reach is left unverified and asked again later, and a page that stops linking back loses its tick." : "Faighidh am frithealaiche seo an duilleag e fhèin, sa chùlaibh, uair san latha air a’ char as motha airson gach cunntais, thar http no https a-mhàin, agus leughaidh e a’ chiad phàirt dhith. Mur ruig e duilleag, fanaidh i gun dearbhadh is thèid feuchainn rithe a-rithist an ceann greis, agus ma sguireas duilleag de cheangal air ais, caillidh i a’ chromag.",
